# duplicate (#566): each expected_*_ddl builder's PRIMARY KEY / FOREIGN KEY tail
# is identical to the SQLite/PostgreSQL sibling it serves (only the integer type
# token differs) and structurally similar to expected_student_course_ddl's own
# tail. Folding these into one generic, name-parameterized builder would compute
# the expected SQL from the same shape as build_junction_sql, which defeats the
# byte-exact regression guard this file exists to be (see its own header
# comment, "A DDL text assertion proves the string we generate" — the assertion
# has to be a literal, independently-written string, not derived).
tests/schema/test_composite_fk_join_sql.cpp:      duplicate
